{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"albinic-agrologic-dolphin","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nOn the Gerrit `Verified` gate, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer` intermittently CRASHES its pytest-xdist worker instead of failing an assertion:\n\n```\nworker 'gw1' crashed while running\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer\n1 failed, 12849 passed, 65 skipped in 1664.64s (0:27:44)\n```\n\nObserved 2026-08-13 on run 31734135055 (change 1731, patchset 2), macos-latest/py3.13 ONLY — the three ubuntu cells passed. There is no traceback and no assertion text, so the whole matrix job reds and the change takes a `Verified -1` it did not earn.\n\n## Why this is not the already-tracked xdist flake\n`c89f-08b1-2e8c-4133` and `fade-ea90-7564-4715` (both closed) cover the same *shape* — an xdist worker dying with no traceback — but on `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted`, a different test with a different cause. This is the wiki-render variant and has no ticket of its own.\n\n## Leading hypothesis (not yet confirmed)\nThe test drives pandoc subprocesses over a corpus and compares rendered output byte-for-byte. Story `271c-e88f-3220-4c9b` recorded exactly this failure mode for a sibling wiki-render test in its ps3 note: the multi-pass corpus test exceeded CI's 300s per-test timeout on the contended macOS lane, and the worker died rather than reporting. macOS runners are the scarcest cell in the org-wide pool (5 concurrent), so contention there is routine. If that is the cause, the fix is about the test's per-unit cost or its timeout budget, not about the renderer.\n\nThis is a hypothesis from the run metadata plus a documented sibling, NOT a confirmed root cause. It needs the `/rebar-debug` treatment: reproduce deterministically (a contended macOS lane, or the per-test timeout lowered locally until it reproduces), confirm the mechanism, then fix the class.\n\n## Evidence it is not caused by the change that surfaced it\n- Change 1734 contains 1731's exact commit plus one more and passed macos-latest/py3.13 with identical renderer code.\n- 1731 touches five files, none runtime: the portability rubric, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and two portability test modules.\n- The full unit suite passed locally on that tree: 12853 passed, 0 failed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The crash is reproduced deterministically and the mechanism named (timeout budget vs. an actual renderer/subprocess fault), with the reproduction recorded here.\n- [ ] The class is fixed, not the instance — if the cause is the per-test budget on a contended lane, every wiki-render test sharing that shape is covered by the same fix.\n- [ ] A `Verified` run on the fixed suite passes the macOS cell, and the fix does not weaken the byte-identity property the test exists to protect.","id":"0078-fa3e-05d1-4e12","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky CI: wiki-render hardening test kills its xdist worker on macOS"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786650105971258001,"uuid":"fef84a97-f915-4a10-a662-de95875f99e2"}